rt":79118,"end":81395,"sha256":"ec57fe1d2b46c1522723af4e33996a83367e38f4ac618f776e47812fb597b84e","extractionMethod":"native_pdf_text","reviewStatus":"extracted_unreviewed"},{"page":35,"start":81398,"end":83652,"sha256":"399991dbc4156a37d0c8ecab44b0e8222864bfc9e0f91668e4860e24bd9b40dd","extractionMethod":"native_pdf_text","reviewStatus":"extracted_unreviewed"},{"page":36,"start":83655,"end":85412,"sha256":"a9b9bc5413edc55e0a1df9afd1b6827185ddbeed3f07391f5dc244169f32a6de","extractionMethod":"native_pdf_text","reviewStatus":"extracted_unreviewed"}],"pageCount":36},"seedPayloadSha256":"5530a2db86bfb783801dace2f36c8c2c4df1816e117355afd3adcaaab1d035af"}},"extracted_text":"Statistical Review \nSTN: 125757/0 \n \n\n(b) (4)\n\nApplication Type \nBLA \nSTN \n125757/0 \nCBER Received Date \nAugust 26, 2022 \nPDUFA Goal Date \nApril 26, 2022 \nDivision / Office \nDVRPA/OVRR \nCommittee Chair \nGirish Ramachandran, PhD, Christina Houck \nClinical Reviewer(s) \nJoohee Lee, MD \nProject Manager \nChristina Houck, Qun Wang, PhD  \nPriority Review \nYes \nReviewer Name(s) \nZhong Gao, Ph.D. \nMathematical Statistician \nTherapeutics Evaluation Branch 2, DB/OBPV \nReview Completion Date / Stamped Date \n \n \n \nSupervisory Concurrence \nLihan Yan, Ph.D. \nChief, Therapeutics Evaluation Branch 2, \nDB/OBPV \n \n \n \n \nJohn Scott, Ph.D. \nDirector, Division of Biostatistics, OBPV \n \n \n \nApplicant  Seres Therapeutics, Inc. \nEstablished Name \nPurified Microbiome Therapeutic, \n \n(Proposed) Trade Name \nVOWST \nPharmacologic Class \n \nFormulation(s), including Adjuvants, etc. \nPurified microbiome therapeutic \nDosage Form(s) and Route(s) of \n\nAdministration  \n\nCapsules: Each capsule contains a minimum of 1 × \n106 spore colony-forming units (SCFU). For oral \nadministration \nDosing Regimen \nThe recommended dose is 4 capsules taken orally \nonce daily on an empty stomach prior to the first \nmeal of the day for 3 consecutive days. \n Indication(s) and Intended Population(s) \nTo prevent the recurrence of Clostridioides difficile \ninfection (CDI) in adults with recurrent CDI \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \nPage i \n\n\f\nStatistical Review \nSTN: 125757/0 \n \n\nTable of Contents \n\nList of Tables ..................................................................................................................... 4 \n\nList of Figures .................................................................................................................... 4 \n\nList OF ABBREVIATION ............................................................................................... 5 \n\n1. Executive Summary ...................................................................................................... 6 \n\n2. Clinical and Regulatory Background ......................................................................... 6 \n\n2.1 Disease or Health-Related Condition(s) Studied .......................................................................... 6 \n2.2 Currently Available, Pharmacologically Unrelated Treatment(s)/Intervention(s) for the \nProposed Indication(s) ................................................................................................................... 6 \n2.4 Previous Human Experience with the Product (Including Foreign Experience) ....................... 7 \n2.5 Summary of Pre- and Post-submission Regulatory Activity Related to the Submission .......... 7 \n2.6 Other Relevant Background Information ..................................................................................... 7 \n\n3. Submission Quality and Good Clinical Practices ...................................................... 7 \n\n3.1 Submission Quality and Completeness .......................................................................................... 7 \n3.2 Compliance With Good Clinical Practices And Data Integrity ................................................... 7 \n\n4. Significant Efficacy/Safety Issues Related to Other Review Disciplines.................. 7 \n\n5. Sources of Clinical Data and Other Information Considered in the Review .......... 7 \n\n5.1 Review Strategy ............................................................................................................................... 7 \n5.2 BLA/IND Documents That Serve as the Basis for the Statistical Review ................................... 7 \n5.3 Table of Studies/Clinical Trials ...................................................................................................... 8 \n5.4 Consultations ................................................................................................................................... 9 \n\n5.4.1 Advisory Committee Meeting (if applicable) .......................................................................... 9 \n5.4.2 External Consults/Collaborations (if applicable) .................................................................... 9 \n5.5 Literature Reviewed (if applicable) ............................................................................................... 9 \n\n6. Discussion of Individual Studies/Clinical Trials ........................................................ 9 \n\n6.1 Study SERES-012 ............................................................................................................................ 9 \n\n6.1.1 Objectives (Primary, Secondary, etc) ...................................................................................... 9 \n6.1.2 Design Overview ................................................................................................................... 10 \n6.1.3 Population ............................................................................................................................. 10 \n6.1.4 Study Treatments or Agents Mandated by the Protocol ........................................................ 10 \n6.1.6 Sites and Centers ...............................................................................